                    {
                        "sense_id": "82c29220-ca6d-3909-b85e-74963b8674b7",
                        "entry_id": "1b565faf-25f1-3546-899b-475c5f5ad176",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Nervous, tense, jumpy."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively",
                            "uncommon"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e7afc429-b067-4705-b8b1-5853705bd0ea",
                                "sense_id": "82c29220-ca6d-3909-b85e-74963b8674b7",
                                "text": "Everyone else Christian had had anything to do with, ever since the bad night outside Alexandria, had seemed to be overwound, jumpy, bitter, hysterical, overtired..."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "287ceeb4-dea4-405a-8b7e-1b2de2f3379c",
                                "sense_id": "82c29220-ca6d-3909-b85e-74963b8674b7",
                                "text": "He has left his class, at least in spirit, by being in certain ways unusual; and he is still unusual in another class, too tense and overwound."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5cf3e1e4-e773-49ba-b189-affaa2c7643f",
                                "sense_id": "82c29220-ca6d-3909-b85e-74963b8674b7",
                                "text": "Eric's boss had accused him more than once of being a worrier, but Eric hadn't felt this overwound since his previous employer's stock underwent a dot-bomb implosion."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6b016af6-69ff-4179-95b7-98fe3ae85cfd",
                                "sense_id": "82c29220-ca6d-3909-b85e-74963b8674b7",
                                "text": "He [Cheney] could only exist with a chief executive self-absorbed in his resentments, narrow in experience and intellectual scope, and who does not hold his vice president accountable; an incompetent national security advisor, overwound in her eagerness to please; and a secretary of state who never presses his advantages but accepts his internal defeats, playing the good soldier."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
